From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:05:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] R5: ChromiumVideoRenderer, the real video adapter behind
 the port (not wired: R6)

Opens RENDER_WEB_ORIGIN/render/<token> in its own headless Chromium (own profile folder, fresh context of the request's size), the web's stepped
clock frozen from the page's first script (read from RENDER_CLOCK_PATH, never copied; optional sha256 pin; a spec checks its contract), steps 1/30 s,
pipes frames to ffmpeg (H.264 yuv420p, no sound, faststart), one short segment per scene joined without re-encoding so IK6a's cut keeps the opening and
the ending whole. Abort and child crashes kill Chromium (by group) and ffmpeg by PID and remove every temp file. Host allowlist, metadata address
always blocked, token masked in every message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
