Subject: [PATCH 2/3] R5 round 1: egress proxy, repeatable clock, fetched clock
 with self-check, abort and encoder fixes

H1 (IK6d): Chromium runs through a proxy the adapter owns (host AND port, metadata in every form,
plain-text tunnels refused); WebSocket closed in the browser; no workers; WebRTC and QUIC off.
M2: every wait of the start races the abort; zombies no longer count as left behind.
M3 (IK6f): clock frozen from the first script at epochMs; first frame waits for fonts and pictures;
stepped time moves only while no request is in flight.
M4: the web clock's timer errors are page errors; proved through the adapter.
M5 (IK6e): clock script fetched from the web origin at each render (256 KB, JavaScript type, allow-list),
checked in a blank page (clock drift); nothing from the website is imported or run by node.
L7: an encoder that dies while flushing fails the render at once. L8: plain words for a same-host
navigation and a broken clock file.

